From ec003017df30f5ac0125042673b7a4663458327f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabio Baltieri <fabiobaltieri@google.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 19:30:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: led: add a Linux LED native_sim driver

Add a native_sim driver to control a Linux LED on the host using the
Zephyr LED APIs.

Signed-off-by: Fabio Baltieri <fabiobaltieri@google.com>
---
 boards/native/native_sim/doc/index.rst        |  20 ++
 drivers/led/CMakeLists.txt                    |   8 +
 drivers/led/Kconfig                           |   1 +
 drivers/led/Kconfig.linux-leds                |  13 ++
 drivers/led/linux_leds.c                      | 196 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../led/zephyr,native-linux-leds.yaml         |  37 ++++
 tests/drivers/build_all/led/app.overlay       |  12 ++
 7 files changed, 287 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/led/Kconfig.linux-leds
 create mode 100644 drivers/led/linux_leds.c
 create mode 100644 dts/bindings/led/zephyr,native-linux-leds.yaml

diff --git a/boards/native/native_sim/doc/index.rst b/boards/native/native_sim/doc/index.rst
index ee26998f6f82..18a13c9fa26f 100644
--- a/boards/native/native_sim/doc/index.rst
+++ b/boards/native/native_sim/doc/index.rst
@@ -543,6 +543,26 @@ Here are more details on the peripherals that are currently provided with this b
 
   SocketCAN support can be enabled by using the :ref:`snippet-socketcan-native-sim`.
 
+**LED device**
+  Implements a Zephyr LED device backed by a Linux LED. You configure which
+  Linux LED to use by setting the DT ``path`` property to the name of the LED
+  as it shows in ``/sys/class/leds``.
+
+  .. code-block:: dts
+
+      leds {
+        compatible = "zephyr,native-linux-leds";
+
+        led0: led_0 {
+          /* /sys/class/leds/tpacpi::lid_logo_dot/brightness */
+          path = "tpacpi::lid_logo_dot";
+        };
+        led1: led_1 {
+          /* /sys/class/leds/tpacpi::power/brightness */
+          path = "tpacpi::power";
+        };
+      };
+
 .. _native_ptty_uart:
 
 PTY UART
